  "Question": "Suppose that the euro is worth \\(1.30\\) dollars. If Diana has \\(500\\) dollars and Étienne has \\(400\\) euros, by what percent is the value of Étienne’s money greater than the value of Diana’s money?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(6.5\\)",
    "D": "\\(8\\)",
    "E": "\\(13\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "First express both amounts in dollars. Étienne's \\(400\\) euros are worth\n\\[\n400\\cdot1.30=520\n\\]\ndollars, which is \\(520-500=20\\) dollars more than Diana has.\n\nThe question compares this excess with Diana's money, so the percentage uses \\(500\\) as its base:\n\\[\n\\frac{20}{500}=0.04=4\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{4\\%}\\), choice B.",
